About Baringa&nbsp;

Baringa is a global consulting firm that partners with leaders to drive change and create value. With deep industry expertise, and enabled by advanced technology, the firm helps clients to deliver with greater confidence and certainty. With over 2,000 people across the UK, Europe, North America, Asia and Australia, the firm combines global insight with local understanding.

The firm works across energy and resources, financial services, government and public sector, consumer products and retail, pharmaceuticals and life sciences, manufacturing, and technology, media and telecoms, with capabilities spanning strategy, transformation and operational excellence - all powered by advanced technology, data, AI and digital innovation.

Clients value Baringa’s collaborative approach and the way its teams integrate seamlessly - all working with a shared understanding of what matters most. The firm is known for its kind, curious experts who listen closely and care deeply about client success as they help clients transform energy markets, modernise financial platforms, expand telecoms and digital networks through advanced data analytics, enable digital services in government, and unlock growth in consumer sectors.

Certified as a&nbsp; Great Place to Work around the world, Baringa has been recognised by the Financial Times in 22 categories of its UK Leading Management Consultants rankings, and by Forbes for four consecutive years as one of the World’s Best Management Consulting Firms.

Our Sector Business Management team are looking for someone to join them.

The Sector Business Management team has a very wide range of activities supporting the realisation of strategic priorities, from supporting recruitment and business development through to identifying margin leakage and opportunities for improved resource utilisation.&nbsp; These roles benefit from the full support of the wider Baringa Enablement team, including a wide range of systems and tools, all of which are leveraged fully to the benefit of the sector or geography in question. &nbsp; &nbsp;

What you will be doing

• Support the COO and Sector lead in the delivery of their objectives and in the coordination of sector-wide activities and communications (e.g. strategy updates, OKRs)&nbsp;

• Steer the leadership team towards the achievement of the sector objectives - with emphasis on strategic priorities, rather than day to day operations - by driving conversation, offering constructive, challenging questions &amp; probes and managing the agenda and governance of the leadership forums&nbsp;

• Support the COO in regular review and reporting of progress towards agreed strategic priorities (through mechanisms such as the OKR framework) , including developing and sharing management information and insights, leadership communications and so on&nbsp;

• Support the Sector COO and leadership team through the management of sector level data sets and sourcing of information from which relevant insights and management information can be drawn.&nbsp; Work closely with Sector and central teams to marry local MI/KPI reporting requirements with the availability and cadence of data from centrally managed systems and tools, avoiding duplication of reporting or analysis.&nbsp;&nbsp;

• Support the Sector leadership with revenue / margin growth, ensuring that key operational activities (e.g. rate card reviews, pricing models, strategic account reviews etc.) are effectively carried out and outcomes implemented.&nbsp;&nbsp;

• Work with the leadership team and Baringa Enablement Marketing team to keep the sector aligned and on track to its committed campaigns and commercial and marketing plans&nbsp;

